``\n   \n   - **`cmd/basename/basename_test.go`** (does NOT exist yet, needs creation)\n     - Glob confirmed no test file exists\n     - Must create with TestDiff function following the differential testing pattern\n   \n   - **`pkg/testutils/difftest.go`** (read for contract understanding)\n     - `DiffTest` struct: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n     - `RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)` runs each test as a subtest\n     - Compares stdout, stderr, and exit codes between Go and reference binaries\n     - `buildEnv` sets LC_ALL=C by default\n   \n   - **`pkg/testutils/build.go`** (read for contract understanding)\n     - `BuildBinary(t, dir)` compiles Go package and returns binary path\n     - Uses `t.TempDir()` for output location\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - only file reading was performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the test file doesn't exist and needs to be created from scratch\n   - Identified that main.go may need --help/--version support for differential test parity with gbasename, though the SRD doesn't explicitly require these flags\n   - The existing main.go already implements all R1-R3 functionality correctly\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: Extremely detailed stitch task description with full project context, SRDs, architecture, constitutions, package contracts, and task requirements for implementing srd015-basename R4.1-R4.3\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - summarization request\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/basename/basename_test.go` with differential tests covering all R4.2 cases\n   - Potentially modify `cmd/basename/main.go` to add --help and --version flag handling if needed for differential test parity\n   - Run `go build ./cmd/basename/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/basename/ -count=1` to verify tests pass or skip gracefully\n\n8. Curren