{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WvKi16LKGzhy8yPfGZMtuQ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive overview. Let me compile my findings in a clear report.\n\nBased on my search of the go-unix-utils repository, I found clear patterns for how cmd/ packages handle --help and --version flags. Here are the key patterns:\n\n## Flag Handling Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Explicit switch/case in main() (true, false, version commands)\n\n**Files:**\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5140/cmd/true/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5140/cmd/false/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5140/cmd/version/main.go`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Uses string constants for help and version text\n- Checks `os.Args[1]` in main() with a switch statement\n- No external flag parsing library (not using `flag` package)\n\n**Key code snippet from true/main.go:**\n```go\nconst helpText = `Usage: true [ignored command line arguments]\n  or:  true OPTION\nExit with a status code indicating success.\n\n      --help     display this help and exit\n      --version  output version information and exit\n`\n\nconst versionText = `true (go-unix-utils) dev\n`\n\nfunc main() {\n\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\n\tif len(os.Args) > 1 {\n\t\tswitch os.Args[1] {\n\t\tcase \"--help\":\n\t\t\tif _, err := fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\tcase \"--version\":\n\t\t\tif _, err := fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Custom flag parsing (basename, cat, sponge)\n\n**Files:**\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5140/cmd/basename/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5140/cmd/cat/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5140/cmd/sponge/main.go`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Implement custom parseArgs/parseFlags functions\n- Manual handling of flag parsing (supporting both short and long flags)\n- Reference to --help in error messages (e.g., \"Try 'basename --help' for more information.\")\n- sponge/main.go uses `flag.Bool` for its -a flag (append mode)\n- cat uses custom parseFlags() that doesn't use the flag package\n\n**Key code from basename/main.go:**\n```go\nfunc parseArgs(args []string) (options, []string, error) {\n\tvar opts options\n\tvar names []string\n\n\ti := 0\n\tfor i < len(args) {\n\t\targ := args[i]\n\t\tif arg == \"--\" {\n\t\t\tnames = append(names, args[i+1:]...)\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--\") {\n\t\t\tn, err := parseLongFlag(arg, args[i:], &opts)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn opts, nil, err\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\ti += n\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif len(arg) > 1 && arg[0] == '-' {\n\t\t\tn, err := parseShortFlags(arg[1:], args[i+1:], &opts)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn opts, nil, err\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\ti += 1 + n\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tnames = append(names, arg)\n\t\ti++\n\t}\n\treturn opts, names, nil\n}\n```\n\n### Exit Codes Used\n\n- **Exit 0**: Success for --help and --version (true, version commands)\n- **Exit 1**: Errors (basename, cat) or for false command regardless of flag\n- **Exit 2**: Unknown option error (version command with unrecognized argument)\n\n### Version Pattern\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5140/cmd/version/main.go`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Exported `Version` variable set to \"dev\" by default\n- Can be overridden via `-ldflags \"-X main.Version=<tag>\"`\n- Used in cmd/version itself and can be referenced by other commands\n- Test verifies this pattern: `TestVersionExported()`\n\n**Code:**\n```go\nvar Version = \"dev\"\n\nfunc main() {\n\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\n\tif len(os.Args) == 1 {\n\t\tfmt.Println(Version)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tswitch os.Args[1] {\n\tcase \"--version\", \"-v\":\n\t\tfmt.Println(Version)\n\tdefault:\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Usage: version [--version | -v]\")\n\t\tos.Exit(2)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n### No pkg/sys Pattern\n\n**Finding:** There is no common help/version handling utility in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5140/pkg/sys/`. The sys package only contains:\n- signal.go (SIGPIPE handler)\n- sigpipe.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler function)\n- stat_darwin.go\n- terminal.go\n- fileinfo.go\n\nEach command implements its own approach to --help and --version handling."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"42687951-365f-454b-a978-a292460ae6b8","uuid":"91645fab-3707-46c1-b955-a6663ee4b3be","timestamp":"2026-05-14T03:47:32.613Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5140, search for how other cmd/ packages handle --help and --version flags. Look at a few cmd/*/main.go files that exist and have actual content. Also check if there's a pattern in pkg/sys or similar for version/help output. Report the patterns you find with file paths and relevant code snippets. Search breadth: medium.","agentId":"ab7e1dd383d5d426b","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive overview. Let me compile my findings in a clear report.\n\nBased on my search of the go-unix-utils repository, I found clear patterns for how cmd/ packages handle --help and --version flags. Here are the key patterns:\n\n## Flag Handling Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Explicit switch/case in main() (true, false, version commands)\n\n**Files:**\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5140/cmd/true/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5140/cmd/false/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5140/cmd/version/main.go`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Uses string constants for help and version text\n- Checks `os.Args[1]` in main() with a switch statement\n- No external flag parsing library (not using `flag` package)\n\n**Key code snippet from true/main.go:**\n```go\nconst helpText = `Usage: true [ignored command line arguments]\n  or:  true OPTION\nExit with a status code indicating success.\n\n      --help     display this help and exit\n      --version  output version information and exit\n`\n\nconst versionText = `true (go-unix-utils) dev\n`\n\nfunc main() {\n\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\n\tif len(os.Args) > 1 {\n\t\tswitch os.Args[1] {\n\t\tcase \"--help\":\n\t\t\tif _, err := fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\tcase \"--version\":\n\t\t\tif _, err := fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Custom flag parsing (basename, cat, sponge)\n\n**Files:**\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5140/cmd/basename/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5140/cmd/cat/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5140/cmd/sponge/main.go`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Implement custom parseArgs/parseFlags functions\n- Manual handling of flag parsing (supporting both short and long flags)\n- Reference to --help in error messages (e.g., \"Try 'basename --help' for more information.\")\n- sponge/main.go uses `flag.Bool` for its -a flag (append mode)\n- cat uses custom parseFlags() that doesn't use the flag package\n\n**Key code from basename/main.go:**\n```go\nfunc parseArgs(args []string) (options, []string, error) {\n\tvar opts options\n\tvar names []string\n\n\ti := 0\n\tfor i < len(args) {\n\t\targ := args[i]\n\t\tif arg == \"--\" {\n\t\t\tnames = append(names, args[i+1:]...)\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--\") {\n\t\t\tn, err := parseLongFlag(arg, args[i:], &opts)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn opts, nil, err\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\ti += n\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif len(arg) > 1 && arg[0] == '-' {\n\t\t\tn, err := parseShortFlags(arg[1:], args[i+1:], &opts)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn opts, nil, err\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\ti += 1 + n\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tnames = append(names, arg)\n\t\ti++\n\t}\n\treturn opts, names, nil\n}\n```\n\n### Exit Codes Used\n\n- **Exit 0**: Success for --help and --version (true, version commands)\n- **Exit 1**: Errors (basename, cat) or for false command regardless of flag\n- **Exit 2**: Unknown option error (version command with unrecognized argument)\n\n### Version Pattern\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5140/cmd/version/main.go`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Exported `Version` variable set to \"dev\" by default\n- Can be overridden via `-ldflags \"-X main.Version=<tag>\"`\n- Used in cmd/version itself and can be referenced by other commands\n- Test verifies this pattern: `TestVersionExported()`\n\n**Code:**\n```go\nvar Version = \"dev\"\n\nfunc main() {\n\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\n\tif len(os.Args) == 1 {\n\t\tfmt.Println(Version)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tswitch os.Args[1] {\n\tcase \"--version\", \"-v\":\n\t\tfmt.Println(Version)\n\tdefault:\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Usage: version [--version | -v]\")\n\t\tos.Exit(2)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n### No pkg/sys Pattern\n\n**Finding:** There is no common help/version handling utility in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5140/pkg/sys/`. The sys package only contains:\n- signal.go (SIGPIPE handler)\n- sigpipe.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler function)\n- stat_darwin.go\n- terminal.go\n- fileinfo.go\n\nEach command implements its own approach to --help and --version handling."}],"totalDurationMs":45700,"totalTokens":43963,"totalToolUseCount":21,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":404,"cache_read_input_tokens":41995,"output_tokens":1560,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":404},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1560,"cache_read_input_tokens":41995,"cache_creation_input_tokens":404,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":404,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":9,"searchCount":6,"bashCount":6,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
