{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018EUjPz1npbMgdFY6vZFHJ2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see that no existing test has a normalizer for binary name differences in stderr. Looking at the sponge test, it does manual error comparisons rather than using `RunDiffTests` for error cases.\n\nFor the error cases in the differential tests, I need a normalizer that replaces the binary name prefix. Since the Go binary will say `basename:` and the ref will say `gbasename:`, I can normalize both to the same prefix.\n\nAlso for the \"Try 'basename --help'\" vs \"Try 'gbasename --help'\" line, same issue.\n\nLet me create a normalizer that replaces both binary names with a common placeholder. Something like:\n\n\nCreating a normalizer function that swaps `gbasename` with `basename` throughout the output to handle the binary name differences between the Go and reference implementations.\n\nNow I need to write the test file and add --help and --version support to main.go. For the main.go changes, I'll handle both flags in the long flag parsing logic to print the appropriate text and exit cleanly. Looking at how GNU coreutils handles this, --help and --version should exit immediately regardless of other arguments, so I'll check for them early in main() before the normal argument parsing, stopping the scan at \"--\" to match standard behavior. I'll format the help text to match GNU basename's structure but with the correct command name, and use the same version format as the `true` command. Now I'm ready to write out both files.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1029,"cache_read_input_tokens":34005,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1029},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"unavail